usage: janus list [-h] [--environment ENVIRONMENT]
                  [--project-root PROJECT_ROOT] [--format {table,json}]
                  [--tag TAG] [--domain DOMAIN] [--family {api,catalog,file}]
                  [--enabled-only] [--graph]

List configured sources with their dispatch, state and dependencies, without
running any.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --environment ENVIRONMENT
                        Environment profile name under conf/environments
                        without the .yaml suffix.
  --project-root PROJECT_ROOT
                        Project root used to resolve conf/ and data/ paths.
  --format {table,json}
                        Output format. Defaults to table.
  --tag TAG             List sources carrying this tag; repeat for an any-
                        match filter. Cannot be combined with --domain.
  --domain DOMAIN       List sources in this domain; repeat for an any-match
                        filter. Cannot be combined with --tag.
  --family {api,catalog,file}
                        List only sources of this strategy family.
  --enabled-only        List only enabled sources. Off by default: disabled
                        sources are listed too.
  --graph               Print the dependency graph of the listed sources
                        instead of their rows: the topological order, then
                        every edge with its table and input path.

Filters list exactly the sources they match. Unlike run-all, list never adds
the upstreams a matching consumer depends on: the UPSTREAMS column names them,
and --graph shows the dependency order. An empty listing exits 0. Only the
source registry is read: no environment profile, no plan and no Spark session.
